> I indeed do not understand how the estimated average acceptance probability could be biased towards initial values when there are 1 million warmup iterations.

Because you are not understanding how adaptation works.  As I have explained multiple times, only the term_buffer iterations are used to estimate the final step size.
If you run 1 million warmup iterations you still only have a term_buffer of 100.

> In the cmdstan documentation, it says adapt term_buffer defaults to 50 and in the rstan documentation it says it defaults to 25. Is it supposed to default to 75?

I misspoke -- it's 50.  Rstan sets it to whatever it wants to.

> In any event, neither changing term_buffer to 100 nor gamma to 0.15 separately or together works for the this Gaussian case:

For a 10D IID Gaussian

./normal sample adapt term_buffer=100 gamma=0.15

works fine,

                    Mean     MCSE   StdDev    5%       50%   95%  N_Eff  N_Eff/s    R_hat
accept_stat__    7.8e-01  6.4e-03  2.0e-01  0.38   8.2e-01   1.0   1000    26413  1.0e+00

The dual averaging is very sensitive to the parameters, and pushing gamma up to huge values will not result in better results than a small increase.

