> Do you mean initial values within the term_buffer or initial values of the Markov Chain? I can see how increasing the term_buffer would yield a more precise estimate and if it is heavily skewed, then an imprecise estimate could exhibit the behavior we are seeing in the examples where many acceptance rates close to 1 and a few close to zero. But I don't see how the initial values of the Markov Chain would entail bias for a reasonable warmup size.

No you misunderstanding.  After (n_warmup - term_buffer) iterations the metric is updated for the last time and then warmup continues of term_buffer iterations to learn the step size for the new metric.
The empirical average acceptance probability in this window is noisy, and tends to underestimate the true expectations because the distribution of acceptance probabilities is no where near normal, more
of a Beta (big number, small number).

>
> Yours is working differently than mine. What commit are you working from?

Develop version of CmdStan and Stan.

