Subject: Running Chains in Parallel
Message-ID: <fQaInNYmKGg.hPNFb7TcEgUJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/fQaInNYmKGg/m/hPNFb7TcEgUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For the ensemble samplers, I want to run 4 chains in parallel using something like

for i in {1..4}
do
model stuff
done

and then

bin/print samples*.csv

But I've noticed that when I run it like this the warmup/sample times are a lot slower and more variable than if I were to run the chains sequentially [which is slower in the sense that it would take longer than running them in parallel].

So should I be running them in parallel or not? And if I do run them in parallel, is it ok to use the warmup/sample times or should we just not bother with using the warmup time as a very rough estimate of time to convergence?

