It's easy to choke a machine when you're doing unbuffered
I/O, because it's basically sequential.

Or when you run memory-intensive processes, because
the memory bus capacities aren't nearly as high as the CPU capacities.

And then there's paging issues.  If you hit four processes and
only have four cores, you may run into process-switching issues
with programs other than what you're running.

Safest thing to do is run one process w/o anything else CPU or
memory or network-intensive running (no e-mail, no browsers, etc.)

We really need to get those servers we can dedicate to testing!

- Bob

