How can I tell how many parameters are involved?  All 3 what?
Ah, I think I may have figured it out.  Is it 2^j parameters
plus an intercept?  That'd explain the 3 and why we have
beta[1] to beta[3].

And all I see is i == 1 in what you sent us.  Does that mean just
one parameter?  Is this intercept-only then?

> and the jth group for number of data points per parameter (ranges from 1 to 8 indicating 2^(j+1) data points per parameter).

OK.

