Have you looked at the new code?  It doesn’t seem like you understand the changes.

I have implemented a var_context factory that handles the creation of a var_context
from configuration data (a string) that the interfaces are responsible for implementing,

var_context factory : common config (string) \rightarrow var_context instance

Any function that needs to read something in from an external source (file, environment, etc)
is templated against such an implementation so any interface can use it by giving
any implementation as the template parameter.

The cmdstan implementation, for example, would use the config string as a file name
and read that in, creating a R-format var_context or a JSON var_context.  Once we have
the pattern down it’s easy to add different input formats on an interface-by-interface basis.

